  "coverage": [
    "Both platforms use native aircraft motion and physics to maintain a20..30 horizontal band and separate ordinary6..10/hydra15..20 height bands. A nearby105-high pillar raises ordinary band relative to target81 to30..34. At least100 consecutive native observations per scene verify height/distance and continued tangential travel.",
    "Actual craft NBT save/load at scene tick120 preserves the sampled .6..8 speed. New unit integration converges from inside, outside and coincident starting positions through production acceleration rather than directly assigning positions.",
    "Full78 native helicopter suite retains finite player70mm/Hellfire, phased blasts, projectile/hull collision, source infinite AI ammunition, crew/PvP/events, hover timing and reload. Ordinary and actual multipart Hydra circles require chin-gun shots; Hydra additionally requires live native proxies, reduced parent health and accepted incoming-contact effects. All three new cases preserve player stores.",
    "Actual integrated clients perform source circle travel, brake into the source-timed Hellfire hover, fire one guided missile, accept its target impact, then resume chin gun. Native renderer checks all eight fixed AI rack nodes against actual launch positions and active original mod audio channels."
  ],
  "failuresAndCorrections": [
    "Initial native runs exposed actual residual hover motion after replacing the slower orbit: the old fixed-anchor flight controller pulled back toward its entry point during the short pre-aim wait. The production hover now requests zero translation, braking via existing acceleration with no teleport or direct velocity reset. Final native and client runs verify launch speed below .04.",
    "Old cover fixtures assumed the former circular path: a midpoint cube could intersect the smaller circle airframe, and a fixed world-axis wall could miss the new path. Replaced with empty-interior opaque enclosures around actual targets; noCollision asserts valid target interiors. Occlusion assertions, source timer and no-fire requirements remain.",
    "Friendly-ray fixture moved to an isolated forced-chunk sortie and waits for actual STRAFE state/entity time. It additionally removes the intervening friend and requires real gunfire to resume with the friend unharmed; this is stronger than the old fixed-tick no-shot assertion.",
    "Multipart gun audit found that the AI rejected non-LivingEntity parts after native ray selection. It now resolves parent allegiance and applies an exact animated contact. The strengthened Hydra test then revealed the shared fixture delayed cleanup had discarded owned body proxies; diagnosis recorded real mesh intersections but part isAlive=false. Cleanup now retains parts whose parent belongs to the fixture, and the test requires live parts, real gunfire, health loss and accepted contact effects."
  ],
